---
// What Tramme costs: nothing, and what can cost money besides it
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import PageHead from '../components/PageHead.astro';
import AppLink from '../components/AppLink.astro';
import DownloadLink from '../components/DownloadLink.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { docHref } from '../lib/docs';
import { repoFile } from '../lib/links';
---

<Base title="Pricing, Tramme is free to use" description="Tramme is free to use, in the browser and on the desktop. Only the AI provider you choose for the assistant can cost money, billed by that provider to your own account.">
  <Nav />
  <main>
    <PageHead title="Free to use." lead="There is nothing to buy and no account to create." />
    <section class="wrap body">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>What is free</h2>
        <p>All of it, today: the app in your browser, the desktop app for Windows, macOS and Linux, the command line and the engine. The source is available under the <a href={repoFile('LICENSE')}>Functional Source License</a>: use Tramme for your own films, for clients or inside your company, change it, keep what you make. The licence reserves one thing, offering Tramme itself, or a product with the same functions, to others as a commercial product or service. Each version becomes Apache-2.0 two years after its release.</p>

        <h2>What can cost money</h2>
        <p>Only the AI the assistant talks to. Tramme does not sell it: you connect your own account with a provider (Anthropic, OpenAI, Google Gemini, OpenRouter, Z.AI), and that provider bills its usage to you, at its own prices. The assistant waits for your yes before anything that costs money, such as a transcription.</p>
        <p>You can use Tramme without any AI. The studio's notes and takes need the assistant, but the atelier, the engine and the export do not.</p>

        <h2>What it does not have</h2>
        <p>Tiers, a trial, a watermark on what you export. The <a href={docHref('limits')}>known limits</a> are about what the engine cannot do yet, not about what you have paid.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ctas"><AppLink /><DownloadLink /></div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>

<style>
  .body { display: grid; gap: 32px; margin-top: clamp(40px, 5vw, 64px); }
  .ctas { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: center; gap: 10px; }
</style>
